"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff scheduled for July 15th, 2023. The project has received a $2M budget approval and is currently in the development phase, led by Omar Jensen, following the completion of the design phase. Key milestones include reaching the first major milestone ahead of schedule with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype, with UI enhancements planned for October. The team is expanding with new members specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, machine learning, and cloud computing, including an onboarding session on September 10th. Strategic partnerships have been established with TechInnovate for AI research. Security protocols are being updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget has been increased to $55,000 for training and audits."
